  "description": "Beta: An embeddable holographic voxel/spatial engine for .NET. A chunk of the world is stored as ONE Phasor superposition (position bound to content), not an array of voxels — and level-of-detail is the readout itself: decode with fewer components and the interference blend goes fuzzy, so \"crisp near, dreamy far\" falls out of the math with no discrete LOD meshes and no popping. Decode a chunk as a colour field, a triangulated surface mesh with analytic per-vertex normals, or an argmax block; per-point decode confidence drives an adaptive component budget that spends extra detail only where the world is genuinely ambiguous, and far (step>1) reads spatially average height and material instead of point-sampling, so distant terrain reads as smooth shapes rather than noise. Entities (creatures/props) store and decode the same holographic way via HoloModel, with two ready-made examples (Creatures.Wraith/Crystal). Ships a built-in procedural world generator (WorldGen: wave-based biomes, an Arena/RaceMode/ringworld-periodic terrain, a connected maze of wall structures) and a flat-to-cylinder Ring warp for ringworld render spaces, or implement IWorldSource to drive the engine from your own world data entirely. Truncated holograms make memory scale with perceived detail rather than world size; fused SIMD bind/correlate keep generation and decode allocation-free. Rendering-agnostic (verified headless) and content-agnostic — supply your own block palette. Built on the Phasor VSA codec.",
